\newlabel{fig:curvature}{{2}{7}{\textbf {Curvature horizon.} Determinant density correctly permits one long cell on a straight coherent feature (left). The same tangent span leaves a curved feature by approximately \(\kappa a^2/2\) (center). The multiplicative correction in \cref {eq:curvature} increases population only until each local straight support fits within its normal span (right).\relax }{figure.caption.7}{}}
